{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And to Moses He said: Ascend.</b> After He finished saying כֹּה תֹאמַר אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אַתֶּם רְאִיתֶם (Exodus 20:18), and specified that they should not ascend to Him by means of intermediaries, and that an earthen altar would suffice, together with observance of His commandments as set forth in the Decalogue and in the section of the judgments — Scripture states that He said and commanded all of these collectively to Israel, while to Moses He said that he should ascend, as He had promised him before the giving of Torah, saying לֵךְ רֵד וְעָלִיתָ אַתָּה וְאַהֲרֹן עִמָּךְ (Exodus 19:24)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:04.099585544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}